# TypeScript

- Keep `strict` enabled. Do not add `any` to “make it compile”; use precise types or `unknown` + narrowing.
- Shared action keys, analytics names, and roles live in `packages/shared`, not copy-pasted strings in screens.
- Parse external input (Edge Function bodies, provider payloads) with zod or equivalent. Do not type-assert untrusted JSON.
- Prefer discriminated unions for UI async state: loading | empty | error | success | offline | permission.
- Public env types: only anon/publishable keys. Service-role types must not exist in `apps/mobile`.

```ts
// BAD
const xp = payload.xp as number;

// GOOD
const body = SubmitPredictionSchema.parse(payload);
```
